tools.description:
Report current repo/branch/index status with freshness fields. Use first to check if an index is ready. If status is indexing, wait/retry shortly instead of refreshing immediately.

RETURNS: {repo, branch, headSha, indexId, status, dirtyFiles, lastIndexedAt, indexingStartedAt?, indexingAgeMs?, inGitRepo}

EXAMPLE: cl_current

Delete a specific branch/index explicitly. Refuses the active or pinned index.

RETURNS: {deleted, indexId, reason?}

EXAMPLE: cl_drop(branch: \

Return exact current local file content by path/range. Reads from disk — never stale stored text. Use after cl_search/cl_related to read target snippets before editing.

RETURNS: {path, startLine, endLine, content, truncated, chars}

EXAMPLE: cl_expand(path: \

Blast-radius analysis for a symbol or file in the current branch index. Returns callers, callees, affected files, and affected tests with hops/confidence. Use before changing shared code.

RETURNS: {indexId, target?, candidates?, callers, callees, affectedFiles, affectedTests, depth, confidenceNote, freshness?, pendingFiles?}

EXAMPLE: cl_impact(symbol: \

Load a saved working-context by name. Returns items (path/symbol-based, stable across reindex).

RETURNS: {context, items}

EXAMPLE: cl_load(name: \

Outline / repo-map: per-file symbol signatures for a file or directory, read from the index (no file re-read). Cheap orientation before diving in. Defaults to exported symbols; pass all:true for everything.

RETURNS: {indexId, files:[{path, symbols:[{name,kind,signature,startLine,endLine,exported}]}], fileCount, truncated}

EXAMPLE: cl_map(path: \

Run a manual TTL sweep: delete expired inactive indexes. Never deletes active/pinned/locked/grace-window indexes.

RETURNS: {deletedIndexes, skipped}

EXAMPLE: cl_prune

Create or update the current branch/worktree index. Scans files, indexes FTS, extracts symbols, builds graph. If background auto-index is already running, returns status:indexing instead of duplicating work.

RETURNS: {indexId, branch, indexedFiles, totalChunks, skipped, status, indexingStartedAt?, indexingAgeMs?}

EXAMPLE: cl_refresh

Graph expansion: neighbors of a file (imports/imported_by/tests/callers/inheritance) within the current index, bounded by depth. Compact handles.

RETURNS: {indexId, results:[{handle,path,edgeType,hops,confidence}]}

EXAMPLE: cl_related(path: \

Save a named working-context set (handles/paths + notes) in a separate DB that survives core-index rebuilds. Pin to prevent TTL deletion.

RETURNS: {id, name, pinned, itemCount}

EXAMPLE: cl_save(name: \

Index statistics: file/symbol/chunk/edge/index counts, total indexes, last indexed. Scoped to active index.

RETURNS: {active, indexId, branch, counts, lastIndexedAt, totalIndexes}

EXAMPLE: cl_stats

Global usage statistics across all repos: per-tool call counts, bytes served, estimated context bytes saved, and a per-repo breakdown. Use to see how much the index tools are being used.

RETURNS: {perTool:[...], perRepo:[...], totals:{calls,bytes_served,bytes_saved}}

EXAMPLE: cl_usage
